Z||000004||AusFiero||07-17-2001||12:47 AM||||Wow they charge a lot to recondition them in America don't they. I have a good 86 1/2 GT wheel here (less bosskit but has immaculant horn ring and button, fittings and badging etc, leather is good too bar being smooth on top and one minor split about 1/8" long that you have to look hard to find) and can get it recovered for about $70 US, which includes shipping to another state for one of our countries best steering wheel manufacturers to do the job.<P>So if your interested Stage-2 (love that name  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) I can get it recovered for you and totally reconditioned ready to bolt onto your old bosskit and sell it to you for US$150 which would include shipping and insurance to USA or Canada. <P>Or if your not interested, anybody? I really don't want to just throw it away because the leather is a smooth on top and it can be made as new so easily.<P>I just have no use for it anymore having a custom interior and all.<P>Anyone interested just email me at jim@jadeweb.com.au Stage 2 has first option of course as I just offered it to him.<P>Or if anyone wants it as is drop $70 off the price. I will send pics on request but not today as I am still resting.<P>I won't make much off this, due to shipping, if someone wants it but I would rather see it find a new Fiero to live in rather than a dump.<BR><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
